    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d752">

                <pb facs="1079" n="1065" sameAs="frus:frus1947v05/pg1065"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/3–2647: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tuck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-26T14:00:00+02:00">March 26, 1947—2
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>368. [League of] Arab States at Council meeting Monday night: (1) pledged
                    themselves to defend independence Palestine; (2) authorized establishment League
                    committee to organize such defence; (3) requested member states to supply
                    necessary funds to Higher Arab Committee [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] to
                    intensify Palestine propaganda and to educate Arabs abroad with view of creating
                    Arab university in Palestine; (4) demanded complete and immediate stoppage
                    immigration. Council also protested against inefficient British measures against
                    illegal immigration. Criticism of America and President Truman were dropped from
                    original resolution.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d752-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Council reiterated support of unity and independence of Libya and charged
                    Secretary General of the League to exert every effort to participation of League
                    or Arab states<anchor n="2" xml:id="d752-f2"/> in any inquiry or plebiscite
                    concerning Libya. Embassy advised informally that League is drafting note on
                    this subject.</p>
                <p>Repeated London 25.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tuck</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d752-f1" n="1" xml:id="d752-f1-content">
                <p>The texts of the four resolutions were transmitted to the Department in despatch
                    2385, March 28, from Cairo. The despatch reported that during the Council
                    discussions, the Iraqi delegate advocated drastic action against the United
                    States and Great Britain, amounting to a breaking-off of diplomatic relations.
                    This view was tempered by the other member states (867N.01/3–2847).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d752-f2" n="2" xml:id="d752-f2-content">
                <p>Seemingly garbled; despatch 2385 indicates participation of “the Arab League or
                    some Arab countries” was intended at this point.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
